# Samba installs and self-enables its entire AD/cluster suite; only
# the guest games share (our custom smbd.service) is wanted.
# samba.service is a domain controller, smb.service duplicates our
# unit without the /data ordering, and winbind hangs in "activating"
# forever without a domain - which keeps multi-user.target's start job
# waiting and with it anything ordered after boot completion.
#
# This must be a preset, not an rm in post-build: buildroot runs
# `systemctl preset-all` as a rootfs-pre-cmd hook AFTER post-build,
# and systemd's default policy enables every unit with an [Install]
# section - so deleted symlinks simply come back. preset-all applies
# these disable lines by removing the enablement symlinks, whoever
# created them.
disable samba.service
disable smb.service
disable nmb.service
disable winbind.service
disable ctdb.service
disable samba-bgqd.service

# Nightly BT controller refresh (see bt-refresh.service): timers with
# [Install] need explicit enablement through preset-all too.
enable bt-refresh.timer
